From 1bb313d880cbcaf384ec4905462a4a7939358663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:16:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(setup): per-setup stock source and the incoming
 stock on the setup page

A setup after the first picks where its stock comes from: "Its own stock
(the Stock node)" or "What <previous setup> leaves behind" (the machined
body #317 carries). Stored on SetupDef as Option<StockSource>; unpicked
reads #317's implicit rule (linked or held differently: what the previous
setup leaves; same hold unlinked: its own stock, the M3.2 A clip), so
every existing document simulates, posts and stamps unchanged.

- SetSetupStockSource: undoable, validated at construction (not the first
  setup, a carry the sim can verify, a real change); the pick rides the
  setup's operation stamps, so its operations go Stale.
- Sim: FromPrevious carries; Own keeps the clip in the same hold and
  takes a new block in a different hold. The gouges of a block left
  behind fold into the program verdict, never dropped.
- Setup page: the option enabled from the second setup on; a refused
  carry disables it with the reason; the incoming body's box and volume
  are shown, measured once per document version.
- Setup sheet: STOCK states the source and the incoming box/volume.
- Project v57: "stock_source": "own" | "from_previous"; absent is
  unpicked; an unknown word is corrupt.

Decisions: docs/decisions/320-stock-source.md. Viewport preview: #406.

Fixes #320

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
